{
  "_comment_before_broken_pattern": "This is what causes the reported bug: <!var!> placeholders pass through makeData unresolved. The merge task's data_to_merge references the childJob's job_details output directly, and that merge's merged_object is then wired straight into makeData.incoming.variables. Per SKILL.md builder-agent ### makeData section: 'makeData.incoming.variables cannot use $var references to a merge that sources childJob output' -- the platform cannot compile $var.<mergeId>.merged_object as a taskRef in that specific field when the merge contains a childJob ref, so it is stored as a literal static string instead. Template substitution then runs against the literal string '$var.e1e1.merged_object', not the real object, so every <!var!> placeholder passes through unresolved.",
  "broken_pattern": {
    "tasks": {
      "a1a1": {
        "name": "childJob",
        "canvasName": "childJob",
        "summary": "Provision Subnet (fan out)",
        "location": "Application",
        "locationType": null,
        "app": "WorkFlowEngine",
        "type": "operation",
        "displayName": "WorkFlowEngine",
        "variables": {
          "incoming": {
            "task": "",
            "workflow": "Provision Subnet",
            "variables": {},
            "data_array": "$var.job.subnets",
            "transformation": "",
            "loopType": "parallel"
          },
          "outgoing": { "job_details": null }
        },
        "actor": "job"
      },
      "e1e1": {
        "name": "merge",
        "canvasName": "merge",
        "summary": "BROKEN: merges childJob job_details with a static template string",
        "location": "Application",
        "locationType": null,
        "app": "WorkFlowEngine",
        "type": "operation",
        "displayName": "WorkFlowEngine",
        "variables": {
          "incoming": {
            "data_to_merge": [
              { "task": "a1a1", "variable": "job_details" },
              { "key": "template", "value": { "task": "static", "value": "Subnet Provisioning Report" } }
            ]
          },
          "outgoing": { "merged_object": null }
        },
        "actor": "Pronghorn"
      },
      "f1f1": {
        "name": "makeData",
        "canvasName": "makeData",
        "summary": "BROKEN: variables is a literal string, not a resolved object",
        "location": "Application",
        "locationType": null,
        "app": "WorkFlowEngine",
        "type": "automatic",
        "displayName": "Tools",
        "variables": {
          "incoming": {
            "input": "{\"title\": \"<!template!>\", \"status\": \"<!taskStatus!>\"}",
            "outputType": "json",
            "variables": "$var.e1e1.merged_object"
          },
          "outgoing": { "output": null }
        },
        "actor": "Pronghorn"
      }
    },
    "why_it_fails": "e1e1.data_to_merge contains a childJob reference ({task:'a1a1', variable:'job_details'}). Because of that, $var.e1e1.merged_object cannot be compiled as a taskRef specifically inside makeData.incoming.variables (this limitation is unique to makeData -- query.incoming.obj does not have it). The engine stores the string '$var.e1e1.merged_object' as a literal instead of resolving it, so <!template!> and <!taskStatus!> in makeData.incoming.input are substituted against nothing and come through as literal, unresolved placeholders in the output."
  },

  "_comment_fixed_pattern": "Fix: never feed a childJob-sourced merge directly into makeData.incoming.variables. Extract each individual scalar you need out of the childJob-sourced merge with `query` tasks (query.incoming.obj DOES resolve $var refs to a childJob-sourced merge -- it is only makeData.incoming.variables that cannot). Then build a SECOND, clean merge containing only those already-resolved scalars plus static values (no childJob refs at all), and feed THAT merge's merged_object into makeData.",
  "fixed_pattern": {
    "tasks": {
      "a1a1": {
        "name": "childJob",
        "canvasName": "childJob",
        "summary": "Provision Subnet (fan out)",
        "location": "Application",
        "locationType": null,
        "app": "WorkFlowEngine",
        "type": "operation",
        "displayName": "WorkFlowEngine",
        "variables": {
          "incoming": {
            "task": "",
            "workflow": "Provision Subnet",
            "variables": {},
            "data_array": "$var.job.subnets",
            "transformation": "",
            "loopType": "parallel"
          },
          "outgoing": { "job_details": null }
        },
        "actor": "job",
        "nodeLocation": { "x": 600, "y": 312 }
      },
      "b2b2": {
        "name": "merge",
        "canvasName": "merge",
        "summary": "Capture childJob job_details via taskRef (guards against $var.a1a1.job_details not resolving downstream on some platform versions)",
        "location": "Application",
        "locationType": null,
        "app": "WorkFlowEngine",
        "type": "operation",
        "displayName": "WorkFlowEngine",
        "variables": {
          "incoming": {
            "data_to_merge": [
              { "task": "a1a1", "variable": "job_details" },
              { "task": "static", "value": {} }
            ]
